From 615510727d789c1a9c7790a1096362ea8f4153c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 07:07:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gui tests: routing-rule-remove presses where the click lands,
 not where a box read said

yetone reported the file red now and then alone (#3096); on this side it
was worse: 3 runs of the file alone gave 7, 7 and 9 of 20 cells red
(chromium and webkit, both widths), on the waits after Save and on the
"no more" read of the needs-condition line. Three races:

- the rule's Remove is read back with one count, so a rule whose row
  leaves a frame after the click still counts 1 (yetone's first report);
- Save and the condition are pressed at coordinates taken from a box
  read before the click, and the app's click guard (gui-shell.md, "a
  click never moves") scrolls the view a frame after that read: what an
  earlier click brought in is held where it was, so the view moves under
  the coordinates and the press lands elsewhere. A press on the rule's
  condition once hit the view's bare stretch: the rule kept its
  condition, Save saved it, and the status the test waits for never came;
- the "said no more" read can run a frame before the toggle's redraw
  puts the line away.

Now press waits for a few scroll-free frames (keptStill, the same
put-back the reader's wheel is spared) and lets the locator click: it
checks the hit where the click lands, and again if it must, so a view
moved after the box was read cannot take the press. The two Remove
counts wait for the rule's row to leave, the keyboard path waits for the
same stillness before its Enter, and the needs-condition line waits
hidden before it is judged. With every press landing, the toggle's
redraw now runs the size watch's hold every time, and the browser's own
"ResizeObserver loop" notice rode in on the errors the test collects;
it is the watch's, not the app's, and the page's errors are read as the
group tests read theirs.

Run (macOS arm64, playwright 1.64.1, node --test --test-concurrency=1):
- before, the file alone, 3 runs: 7, 7, 9 of 20 cells red;
- the worst cell (chromium en 1100, red 6 of 6 with the waits alone) is
  green 3 of 3 with the press checking its hit.

Fixes #3096

